  "text": "Moonshot is offering a Kimi K3.1 Pro “Highspeed” version that it says runs 2–3 times faster at twice the price. The exception matters: cached input tokens cost the same on both versions. The standard API price is $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, so the premium applies differently depending on how much input a workload can reuse from cache.\n\nFor a workflow with substantial cached input, the total bill would rise by less than twofold, with the increase depending on uncached input and output volume. A workflow dominated by generated output would face a cost increase closer to the full doubling. That makes the token mix relevant to choosing between the two versions. Moonshot’s advertised speedup gives developers a reason to test Highspeed on latency-sensitive tasks, while measuring response time and total cost together would establish whether the premium is worthwhile for that workload.",
